From 6302457160695d0d635792f8d1a1303ba0a47d45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 06:08:47 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Rotations of batches

For the behaviours generated by the generic-parallel interface, the
rotation functions of the gradients, of the thermodynamic forces and of the
tangent operator blocks rotate all the points with one call of the batch
rotation function, on the default queue of the backend. The rotation
matrices are given as an array (uniform or point by point) or built by MGIS
from 2D or 3D material axes, in the memory of the host: those are refused
for the cuda and hip backends.

GenericParallelIntegrateTest compares the rotations of an orthotropic
behaviour with the ones of the generic interface (uniform matrix, matrices
given point by point, 3D material axes).
